==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|ūwila|lang=goh}}, from a variant of {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*uwwalǭ}} (compare Dutch {{term|uil|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|ûle|lang=fy}}, English {{term|owl|lang=en}}), diminutive of {{m|gem-pro|*uwwǭ}} ‘eagle-owl’ (compare German {{term|Uhu|lang=de}}), of imitative origin or a variant of {{m|gem-pro|*ūfaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ūfǭ}} (compare Swedish {{term|uv|lang=sv}} ‘horned owl’, Bavarian {{term|Auf|lang=bav}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*up-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʔɔɪ̯lə/|lang=de}}
